Negative control for the auth overlay being dismissable (`R7-12`).

Drops the route's own `dismissable` declaration. The overlay still renders, the
journey still collects, and every auth case still passes — but the visitor is
trapped, because `OverlayController` declares `dismissable` as a Boolean prop
absent from its `withDefaults`, and Vue casts an unpassed Boolean to `false`
rather than leaving it undefined. The dialog is therefore handed a hard `false`:
no close control drawn, ESC prevented, backdrop inert. Proven at runtime — a
component with `dismissable: { type: Boolean }` and no default resolves the
absent prop to `false`, while the neighbouring `modal: { type: Boolean, default:
undefined }` resolves to `undefined`.

This is the subtlest kind of regression the round found, because it removes a
line that looks decorative: the meta is the only thing standing between the
overlay and a gate nobody can leave, and nothing else in the tree says so.

Nothing else moves — the chooser, the journey, the hand-off and the cancel
landing are untouched — so a red here is the way out and not a crash.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: auth-overlay.spec.ts — the case asserting the overlay declares itself
dismissable (and, where the controller is mounted for real, that the dialog gets
`dismissable: true` and draws a close control). Every case about which journey
is collected stays GREEN by construction; if they go red too, the control has
been over-applied.

  FOR THE PROVER: authored by the developer seat, which knew the line to mutate;
  it carries no verification run. Apply it blind, confirm the dismissal case
  goes red and the journey cases stay green, then revert.

--- a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/app/pages/overlays/auth.vue
+++ b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/app/pages/overlays/auth.vue
@@ -89,8 +89,7 @@
  */
 definePageMeta({
   name: ROUTE.OVERLAY_AUTH,
-  overlay: OverlayType.MODAL,
-  dismissable: true
+  overlay: OverlayType.MODAL
 });

 const route = useRoute();
